# Evolution — environment template. Copy to .env and fill in what you use.
# NEVER commit .env. Only variable NAMES are ever recorded in telemetry.
#
# The default routing table needs NONE of these. OpenCode Zen's free tier was
# verified serving four models with no Authorization header on 2026-08-26, and
# those are what the shipped chains lead with. Everything below adds capacity,
# a second rate-limit bucket, or a fallback for when Zen's free pool is busy.

# --- Primary route: OpenCode Zen free tier (works keyless) -----------------
# Optional. Zen serves `nemotron-3-ultra-free`, `hy3-free`, `laguna-s-2.1-free`
# and `nemotron-3.5-lightning-free` without a key. A key is needed for Zen's
# paid models, and may lift the `FreeUsageLimitError` that anonymous callers hit
# on `mimo-v2.5-free` and `big-pickle` — that last part is UNVERIFIED here.
OPENCODE_API_KEY=

# --- Strong fallback: NVIDIA NIM ------------------------------------------
# Model ids in the default table were re-checked against NIM's live catalogue
# on 2026-08-26. Serving is unverified — this repo holds no NIM key.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# --- OpenRouter: a second free bucket -------------------------------------
# 25 of OpenRouter's 416 models were priced at $0 on 2026-08-26, including
# `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free`. Its rate limit is a different
# bucket from Zen's, which is the main reason to key it.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Other OpenAI-compatible providers (optional) -------------------------
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Additional free tiers, not in the default table ----------------------
# Each of these hosts an OpenAI-compatible endpoint with a documented free
# tier. They are NOT shipped as profiles because their model catalogues cannot
# be read without a key, and this repo does not put unverified model ids in a
# routing table — that is precisely the failure of 2026-08-26. Add a profile in
# `control_plane/providers/profiles.py` once you hold a key and can read
# `/models`; the doctor will reconcile it from then on. See PROVIDERS.md.
#
#   Groq      https://api.groq.com/openai/v1     (401 without a key)
# GROQ_API_KEY=
#   Cerebras  https://api.cerebras.ai/v1         (403 without a key)
# CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
#   Google AI Studio, OpenAI-compatible surface:
#             https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Local OpenAI-compatible endpoint (optional) --------------------------
# EVOLUTION_LOCAL_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# EVOLUTION_LOCAL_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder

# --- Control plane --------------------------------------------------------
# EVOLUTION_HOST=127.0.0.1
# EVOLUTION_PORT=8000
# EVOLUTION_CLASSIC_PORT=8080
# EVOLUTION_WORKSPACE=./.evolution/workspace
